We focus on pointwise semi-slant submanifolds within warped product and semi-slant Sasakian manifolds. Building upon existing classifications of warped product semi-slant submanifolds in P-Sasakian manifolds, we reestablish and expand these classifications for (α, β)-P-Sasakian manifolds. Furthermore, considering pointwise semi-slant submanifolds in semi-slant Sasakian manifolds to be semi-slant Riemannian or semi-slant semi-conformal semi-slant, we classify and describe their structure. Finally, we present several concrete examples. As a result, the restrictions and classifications presented in Maruthasan and Bullen's work on warped product semi-slant submanifolds in P-Sasakian manifolds are extended and broadened. Meanwhile, the classifications presented in this study are more restrictive and precise in comparison to those found in Kaur et al.'s work on semi-slant Riemannian and semi-slant semi-conformal semi-slant submanifolds. Additionally, the classifications presented in this study are more restrictive and precise in comparison to those found in Kaur et al.'s work on semi-slant Riemannian and semi-slant semi-conformal semi-slant submanifolds. Finally, the classifications presented in this study are more non-degenerate in comparison to Kaur et al.'s work on semi-slant Riemannian and semi-slant semi-conformal semi-slant submanifolds. 

